  "name": "Sun Dance songs (Lakota and Plains Sun Dance)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Songs of the Sun Dance (Wiwanyang Wacipi), the summer renewal ceremony of the Lakota and of the Cheyenne, Arapaho, Shoshone, Blackfoot, Crow and other Plains nations, held over several days in a circular arbor around a central tree. Singers at a large drum carry the dancers through each round while the dancers blow eagle-bone whistles; Teton Sioux Sun Dance songs were among those Frances Densmore recorded on cylinder for Teton Sioux Music. The powwow drum card stands in for the Sun Dance drum.",
